Notebook[{
Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["Symbolic Computing\n\n",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  StyleBox["LT20, 4:00-6:00pm\nWed, 19 March 2003",
    FontSize->24,
    FontWeight->"Bold"]
}], "Title"],

Cell["", "Subtitle"],

Cell["Extended Euclidean Algorithm", "Subtitle"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Another theorem with regarding to GCD gives us away to compute inverse in \
",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`Z\_p\)]],
  " or other field.   "
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Let D be a Euclidean domain and let ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a\)]],
  ", ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`b\)]],
  " \[Element] D (not both zero).  Then there exists elements ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`s\)]],
  ", ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`t\)]],
  " \[Element] D such that\n\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`GCD(a, b)\  = \ s\ a\  + \ t\ b\)]]
}], "Theorem"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "This theorem says GCD of ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a\)]],
  " and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`b\)]],
  " is a linear combination of a and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`b\)]],
  ".  For example.\nGCD(18,30) = 6.  We have\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`6\  = \ s\ 18\  + \ t\ 30\)]],
  ",  with ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`s\  = \ 2\)]],
  ", ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`t\  = \ \(-1\)\)]],
  ". \n\nLet ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`b\)]],
  " be a prime number ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p\)]],
  ", and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(|\)\(a\)\(|\)\(\ \)\(\(<\)\(\ \)\(p\)\)\)\)]],
  ",  then\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`GCD(a, \ p)\  = \ \(1\  = \ 
          s\ a\  + \ t\ \(\(b\)\(.\)\)\)\)]],
  "    Modulo ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p\)]],
  " we get\n1 mod ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p\ \  = \ \((s\ a\  + \ t\ p)\)\ mod\ p\)]],
  "\nor  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`1\  = \ s\ a\ \ mod\ p\)]],
  "\nThus ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`s\)]],
  " is the multiplicative inverse in the field (",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`Z\_p\)]],
  ";*,+).\n\nExtended Euclidean algorithm is like Euclidean algorithm, with \
few more book-keeping. "
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[{
    \( (*\ Return\ {GCD[a, b], \ s, \ t}\ such\ that\ GCD[a, b]\  = \ 
        s*a\  + \ 
          t*\(\(b\)\(.\)\)\ \[IndentingNewLine]*) \
\[IndentingNewLine]\(ExtendedEuclidean[a_, b_]\  := \ 
        Module[{c, c1, c2, d, d1, d2, r, r1, 
            r2}, \[IndentingNewLine]{c, c1, c2}\  = \ {a, 1, \ 
              0}; \ \[IndentingNewLine]{d, d1, d2}\  = \ {b, \ 0, \ 
              1}; \[IndentingNewLine]While[\ 
            d \[NotEqual] \ 0, \[IndentingNewLine]q\  = \ 
              quotient[c, d]; \[IndentingNewLine]r\  = \ 
              c\  - \ q*d; \[IndentingNewLine]r1\  = \ 
              c1\  - \ q*d1; \[IndentingNewLine]r2\  = \ 
              c2\  - \ q*d2; \[IndentingNewLine]{c, c1, c2}\  = \ {d, d1, \ 
                d2}; \[IndentingNewLine]{d, d1, d2}\  = \ {r, \ \ r1, 
                r2}\[IndentingNewLine]]; \[IndentingNewLine]s = \ 
            c1; \[IndentingNewLine]t = c2; \[IndentingNewLine]{c, \ s, \ 
            t}\[IndentingNewLine]];\)\[IndentingNewLine]\[IndentingNewLine] \
(*\ The\ definition\ of\ quotient[]\ depends\ on\ the\ algberaic\ structure\ \
of\ the\ integral\ domain . \ \ For\ integer\ Z, \ 
      we\ have\ built - 
        in\ \(\(function\)\(.\)\)\ *) \), "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    \(quotient[a_, \ b_]\  := \ Quotient[a, b]\)}], "Input"],

Cell["\<\
Again, the extended Euclidean algorithm works for all Euclidean domains when \
the quotient[ ] function is properly defined.

Here is the working of algorithm to input a = 18, b = 30.

Iteration      q     c    c1    c2      d     d1    d2
     0             -    18    1     0       30    0       1   ( a  & b)
     1            0     30   0     1       18     1      0   (c gets d, d \
gets r)
     2            1     18   1     0       12    -1     1 
     3            1     12  -1     1        6     2     -1
     4            2      6    2    -1       0     -5      3   (stop when d = \
0)\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
        StyleBox["Example",
          FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
        StyleBox[":",
          FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
        RowBox[{
          StyleBox["Compute",
            FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
          StyleBox[" ",
            FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
          StyleBox["the",
            FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
          StyleBox[" ",
            FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
          StyleBox["inverse",
            FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
          StyleBox[" ",
            FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
          StyleBox["of",
            FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
          StyleBox[" ",
            FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
          StyleBox["4",
            FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
          StyleBox[" ",
            FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
          StyleBox["in",
            FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
          StyleBox[" ",
            FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
          SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["Z",
              FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], "5"]}]}], 
      StyleBox[
        FormBox[",",
          "TraditionalForm"],
        FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
      StyleBox[\(using\ extended\ Euclidean\ algorithm . \ GCD \((4, 5)\) = 
          1\),
        FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
      StyleBox[",",
        FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
      StyleBox[\(running\ the\ algorithm\ we\ find\ s = \(-1\)\),
        FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
      StyleBox[",",
        FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
      StyleBox[\(t = 1\),
        FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
      StyleBox[" ",
        FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
      StyleBox[",",
        FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
      RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
          StyleBox["so",
            FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
          StyleBox[" ",
            FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
          SuperscriptBox[
            StyleBox["4",
              FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], \(-1\)]}], 
        StyleBox[" ",
          FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
        StyleBox["=",
          FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
        StyleBox[" ",
          FontFamily->"Times New Roman"], 
        StyleBox[\(\(-1\)\ mod\ 5\  = \ \(4. \ \ This\ is\ checked\ because\ \
4*4\ mod\ 5\  = \ 1. \)\),
          FontFamily->"Times New Roman"]}]}]], "Example"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(ExtendedEuclidean[4, 5]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \({1, \(-1\), 1}\)], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["Why the extended Euclidean algorithm works?", "Subtitle"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "The key to understand extended Euclidean algorithm is to note that it is \
always true that ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`c\)]],
  " = ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a*c\_1\)]],
  " + ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`b*c\_2\)]],
  ", i.e., this is a loop invariant.    Before the loop starts, we have for \
this equation,\na = 1*a + 0 b.  At the end of the run, we have GCD[a,b] = a*s \
+ b*t.    \n\nTo show that extended Euclidean algorithm works, we just need \
to show that \n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`c\)]],
  " = ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a*c\_1\)]],
  " + ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`b*c\_2\)]],
  "                                                                    (1)\n\
",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`d\)]],
  " = ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a*d\_1\)]],
  " + ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`b*d\_2\)]],
  "                                                                   (2)\nis \
valid before and after each update.   "
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
  "Show that it is also true that \n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`r\)]],
  " = ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a*c\_1\)]],
  " + ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(b\)\(*\)\)\)]],
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`c\_2\)]],
  ".                                                     (3)"
}], "Exercise"],

Cell["\<\
Because equations (1), (2), and (3) is true in every iteration, it is true \
through out. \
\>", "Text"],

Cell["An example of polynomial GCD over field Q.", "Subtitle"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Let  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a(x)\  = \ 
        48\ x\^3 - 84  x\^2 + 42  x - 36, \[IndentingNewLine]b(
          x)\  = \ \(-4\) x\^3 - 10  x\^2 + 44  x\  - \ 30. \)]],
  "\ncompute ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`GCD[a(x), \ b(x)]\)]],
  ", ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`s(x)\)]],
  " and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{\(t(x)\), ".", Cell[""]}], TraditionalForm]]],
  "\n\nFollowing the extended Euclidean algorithm step by step, we first \
begin with \n",
  Cell[BoxData[{
      FormBox[\(c(x)\  = \ a(x), \ \(c\_1\)(x)\  = \ 
          1, \ \(\(c\_2\)(x)\  = \ 0;\)\), TraditionalForm], 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{\(d \((x)\)\  = \ b \((x)\)\), ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
              SubscriptBox["d", 
                RowBox[{"1", Cell[""]}]], "(", "x", ")"}], " ", "=", " ", 
            "0"}], ",", " ", \(\(d\_2\) \((x)\)\  = \ 1. \)}], 
        TraditionalForm]}]],
  "\nWe compute ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`r(x)\  = \ Mod[a(x), \ b(x)]\)]],
  " and quotient ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`q(x)\)]],
  " by a long division.\n                                               -12   \
",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \)\(\(\[LongLeftArrow]\)\(\ \ \
\)\(q(x)\)\)\)\)]],
  "\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(-4\) x\^3 - 10  x\^2 + 
        44  x - \(\(30\)\(\ \ \)\(\@\(48  x\^3\ \  - \ \ 84 
                   x\^\(\(2\)\(\ \ \)\) + \ \ 42  
                  x\ \  - \ \ 36\)\)\(\ \)\)\)]],
  "\n                                             48 ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`x\^3\ \  + \ 120\ x\^2\  - 528  x\  + 360\)]],
  "\n                                            __________________________\n \
                          ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(r(x)\)\(\ \)\(\[LongRightArrow]\)\)\)]],
  "                ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(-204\) x\^\(\(2\)\(\ \ \ \)\) + 570  x\  - 
        396\)]],
  "\n\nThus, after first iteration, we have  (replace c by d, replace d by r \
= c - q*d)\n",
  Cell[BoxData[{
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          
          RowBox[{\(c(x)\  = \ b(x)\), ",", " ", \(\(c\_1\)(x)\  = \ 0\), ",",
             " ", 
            RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
                RowBox[{
                  SubscriptBox["c", 
                    RowBox[{"2", Cell[""]}]], "(", "x", ")"}], " ", "=", " ", 
                "1"}], ";"}]}], " "}], TraditionalForm], 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{\(d \((x)\)\  = \ \(r \((x)\)\  = \ \(-204\) x\^2 + 
                570  x\  - 396\)\), ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{\(\(d\_1\)(x)\), " ", "=", 
            RowBox[{\(\(r\_1\)(x)\), " ", "=", " ", 
              SubscriptBox["1", Cell[""]]}]}]}], TraditionalForm], 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{\(\(d\_2\) \((x)\)\), " ", 
          SubscriptBox[
            SubscriptBox["=", Cell[""]], Cell[""]], 
          RowBox[{\(\(r\_2\)(x)\), "=", 
            RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"0", "-", 
                RowBox[{\((\(-12\))\), "*", "1", Cell[""]}]}], "=", " ", 
              "12"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]}]],
  "\n\nNow we are in the second iteration, and do a long division of ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`c(x)\)]],
  " by ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`d(x)\)]],
  ", similar to above, we obtain have\n                                       \
   ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(4\/204\) x\ \ \ \ \ \  + \ 4320\/204\^2\)]],
  "\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(-204\) x\^2 + 570  x - 
        396\ \ \@\(\(\ \ \ \)\(\(-4\) x\^\(\(3\)\(\ \ \)\)\  - \ \ \ 10  x\^2\
\ \ \  + \ \ \ 44  x\ \ \  - \ \ \ 30\)\)\)]],
  "\n                                           ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(-4\) x\^3\  + \(2280\/204\) x\^2 - \(1584\/204\) 
          x\)]],
  "\n                                           ____________________________\n\
                                                 ",
  Cell[BoxData[{
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(-\(4320\/204\)\) x\^2\ \  + \(10560\/204\) 
          x\ \ \ \  - \ 30\), "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(-\(4320\/204\)\) x\^2 + \(2462400\/204\^2\) x - 
        1710720\/204\^2\)}]],
  "\n                                                  \
________________________\n                                                    \
             ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(-\(308160\/204\^2\)\) x\  + 462240\/204\)]],
  "\nReduce to lowest terms for the fraction with GCD computation over \
integer, we find\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(q(x)\)\(\ \)\(=\)\(\ \)\)\)]],
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(\(1\/51\) x\)\(\ \)\(+\)\)\)]],
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`30\/289\)]],
  ",\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`r(x)\  = \ \(-\(2140\/289\)\) x\  + 3210\/289\)]],
  "\nThus new values for ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`c, \ c\_1, \ c\_2\)]],
  " are\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(c(x)\)\(\ \)\(=\)\(\ \)\)\)]],
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(\(-204\) x\^2 + 570  x\  - 396\)\(,\)\)\)]],
  "\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(\(c\_1\)(x)\)\(\ \)\(=\)\(\ \)\)\)]],
  "0, ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(c\_2\)(x)\  = \ 1. \)]],
  "\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`d(
          x)\  = \ \(r(x)\  = \(-\(2140\/289\)\) x\  + 
            3210\/289\), \[IndentingNewLine]\(d\_1\)(
          x)\  = \ \ \(\(-\ \(q(x)\)\)\  = \ \(-\(1\/51\)\) x\  - 
            30\/289\), \[IndentingNewLine]\(d\_2\)(x)\  = \ 
        1 - \ \(q(x)\)*12\)]],
  "\n\nThe third and also the last iteration we do\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(-\(2140\/289\)\) x\  + 3210\/289\)]],
  "  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\@\(\(\(-204\) x\^2\)\(+\)\(570  x\)\(\ \)\(+\)\(396\
\)\(\ \ \)\)\)]],
  "\nand find \n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`q(x)\  = \(14739\/535\) x - 19074\/535, \ \ r(
          x)\  = \ 0\)]],
  "\n\nThus ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`GCD(a, b)\  = \ \(\(c(x)\)\(\ \)\(=\)\(\ \)\)\)]],
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(\(-\(2140\/289\)\) x\  + 3210\/289\)\(,\)\)\)]],
  "\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
            SubscriptBox[\(c\_1\), 
              RowBox[{Cell[""], Cell[""]}]], "(", "x", ")"}], " ", "=", 
          " ", \(\(s(x)\)\(\ \)\(=\)\(\ \)\)}], TraditionalForm]]],
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(-\(1\/51\)\) x\  - 30\/289\)]],
  ",\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(c\_2\)(
          x)\  = \ \(t(
            x)\  = \(\(\(-\ \(12\/51\)\) 
              x\)\(\ \)\(-\)\(71\/289\)\(\ \)\)\)\)]]
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Note that the fractions gets bigger and bigger during iterations.  The \
computation is simpler in a finite field, e.g., in (",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`Z\_p\)]],
  "; +, *)."
}], "Text"],

Cell["Nonuniqueness of GCD", "Subtitle"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "If ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`c\)]],
  " is the greatest common divisor in an integral domain D, so is any  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`u\ *c\)]],
  " for any member ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`u\)]],
  " such that ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`u\^\(-1\)\)]],
  "exists.  Such members are called units.  Since if ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          FormBox["c",
            "TraditionalForm"], "|", "a"}], TraditionalForm]]],
  " and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`c | b\)]],
  ",  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\((u*c)\)\)]],
  " | ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a\)]],
  " is the same as c | ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(u\^\(-1\)\) \(\(a\)\(.\)\)\)]],
  "  In Z (the set of integers), only ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`-\)]],
  "1 and 1 have inverse, so if ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`c\)]],
  " is a GCD, so is ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(-c\)\)]],
  ".   In Q[",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`x\)]],
  "] (the set of polynomials with rational coefficients),  all zeroth-order \
polynomial ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a(x)\  = \ a\_0\)]],
  " for ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a\_0 \[NotEqual] \ 0\)]],
  "  is a unit.  So all GCDs are related by a multiplicative constants.\n"
}], "Text"],

Cell["GCD of Polynomial over Z", "Subtitle"],

Cell["\<\
GCD of polynomial over Z is complicated as Z[x] is not an Euclidean domain, \
thus Euclidean algorithm cannot be applied. This is because the division \
property
a = b*q + r
does not hold for Z[x].    But a similar property known as pseudo-division \
allows GCD to be computed within Z[x].\
\>", "Text"],

Cell["Some Applications of GCD", "Subtitle"],

Cell["\<\
GCD computation is one of the basic computation in a symbolic algebraic \
system.  GCD computation is required for:
\t1. simplifying polynomial rational functions;
\t2. factor of polynomials;
\t3. symbolic integration of polynomial rational functions;
\t4. inverse of extension fields.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "An example of GCD over ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`Z\_p\)]]
}], "Subtitle"],

Cell["Modulo arithmetic", "Subsubtitle"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "If ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a, b, c, \ d\)]],
  " \[Element] Z, we have the following properties regarding operations \
modulo ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p\)]],
  ". These show the relation between the integral domain (Z;+,*) and field \
(",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`Z\_p\)]],
  "; +,*).  Note that each element in Z is mapped to ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`Z\_p\)]],
  " by taking the modulo ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(p\)\(.\)\)\)]]
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "0.\t",
  Cell[BoxData[{
      \(TraditionalForm\`\((a + b)\)\ mod\ p\  = \ \((a\ mod\ p\  + \ 
              b\ mod\ p)\)\ \ mod\ p\), "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      \(TraditionalForm\`\((a*
              b)\)\ mod\ p\  = \ \((\((a\ mod\ p)\)\ *\ \((b\ mod)\)\ p\ )\)\ \
mod\ p\), "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      \(TraditionalForm\`\)}]],
  "\n1.\t",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a\  = \ b\ mod\ p\)]],
  "   implies   ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a - b\)]],
  " is a multiple of ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(p\)\(.\)\)\)]],
  "\n\n2.\tIf ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a\  = \ b\)]],
  " mod ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p\)]],
  ", and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`c = \ d\ mod\ p\)]],
  ", then\n\t",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a\  + \ c\  = \ 
        b\  + \ d\ mod\ p, \[IndentingNewLine]a*c\  = \ b*d\ mod\ p\)]],
  "\n\t\n3.\t",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a\ *\ x\  = \ b\ mod\ p\)]],
  "  has solution  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`x\  = \ a\^\(-1\)*b\)]],
  " mod ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p\)]],
  ",  where ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a\^\(-1\)\)]],
  " is the multiplicative inverse in the field ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`Z\_p\)]],
  ". "
}], "Theorem"],

Cell[TextData[{
  " Note that in Z there is no inverse for an integer except ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(-1\)\)]],
  " and 1.  \nThe relation between Z and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`Z\_p\)]],
  " is known as a ring morphism."
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Consider again the polynomials above:\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a(x)\  = \ 
        48\ x\^3 - 84  x\^2 + 42  x - 36, \[IndentingNewLine]b(
          x)\  = \ \(-4\) x\^3 - 10  x\^2 + 44  x\  - \ 30. \)]],
  "\n\nAssuming that the integers and variable ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`x\)]],
  " live in ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`Z\_p\)]],
  ", we have (after modulo by 5 of the coefficients)\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a(x)\  = \ 
        3  x\^3 + x\^2 + 2  x + 4, \[IndentingNewLine]b(x)\  = \ 
        x\^3 + 4 \( \(x\)\(.\)\)\)]],
  "\n\nA long division would like this:\n                                3\n  \
          ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`x\^3 + 
        4  x\ \ \ \ \@\(3  x\^\(\(3\)\(\ \ \ \)\) + \ \ \ x\^\(\(2\)\(\ \ \ \
\)\) + \ \ \ 2\ x\ \ \ \ \  + \ \ \ \ 4\)\)]],
  "\n                               ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`3  x\^3\  + \ 0  x\^2\ \ \  + \ \ 2  x\)]],
  "\n                               ______________________\n                  \
                          ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(\ \ \)\(x\^2\ \ \  + \ \ \ \ 0\ \ \ \ \  + \ \ \ \
\ 4\)\)\)]],
  "\nOne more division\n                                   ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`x\)]],
  "\n                  ",
  Cell[BoxData[{
      \(TraditionalForm\`x\^2 + 
        4\ \ \ \@\(x\^3\ \  + \ \ \ \ 0\ x\^2\ \ \  + \ \ \ 4\ x\ \ \ \ \  + \
\ \ \ 0\)\), "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      \(TraditionalForm\`\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\^3\ \ \ \  \
+ \ \ 0\ x\^2\ \ \ \  + \ \ \ 4\ x\)}]],
  "\n                                ________________________\n               \
                                                              0\nThus \
GCD(a(x),b(x)) in ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          FormBox[\(Z\_5\),
            "TraditionalForm"], "[", "x", "]"}], TraditionalForm]]],
  " is ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(x\^2 + 4\)\(,\)\)\)]],
  " which is quite different from the results in Q",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\([x]\)\)]],
  ".                        "
}], "Text"]
}, Open  ]]
},
FrontEndVersion->"4.1 for Microsoft Windows",
ScreenRectangle->{{0, 1024}, {0, 695}},
WindowSize->{1016, 668},
WindowMargins->{{1, Automatic}, {Automatic, -2}},
Magnification->3,
StyleDefinitions -> "Classroom.nb"
]

